        "node_id": "n_1_f5da82",
        "thought_text": "Model the problem as a directed graph where each house is a node and there's a directed edge from house x to house p_x. Analyze the strongly connected components (SCCs) of this graph to understand the movement constraints. The condition that starting from any house from 1 to k leads to house 1 suggests that these houses must be part of an SCC that includes house 1. Conversely, houses from k+1 to n should not be part of such an SCC.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
